WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:06.850
It's amazing what ridiculous stories get passed
around the table at a dinner party, or when

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:08.690
you're out drinking with your friends.

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:13.610
I'm sure you've heard a few gruesome tales
that sound too horrible to be true.

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:17.721
Most urban legends are no more than Chinese
whispers; told over and over again, until

00:00:17.721 --> 00:00:21.410
no one can actually remember if there's any
truth to the damn thing.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:27.050
But very occasionally, it turns out that one
of these creepy tales is actually, completely

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:33.239
true and the real-life version is more horrific
than you could ever imagine.

00:00:33.239 --> 00:00:37.140
The Green Man

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:42.570
If you spend long enough in western Pennsylvania,
you will undoubtedly hear the spine-chilling

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:44.890
tales of "The Green Man".

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:50.710
According to the urban legends, he was a horrifically
disfigured man, with no face and glowing,

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:51.710
green skin.

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:55.739
The Green Man apparently wandered the streets
of Pennsylvania every night.

00:00:55.739 --> 00:01:00.210
Drivers would often report seeing this terrifying
figure at the side of the road in the dead

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:01.610
of the night.

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:06.610
Turns out the real story is actually one of
misfortune and loneliness.

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:12.289
The Green Man was not a monster at all but
a man named Raymond Robinson.

00:01:12.289 --> 00:01:17.170
When Robinson was eight years old, he was
attempting to view a birds nest and was electrocuted

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:20.349
by some electrical lines of a nearby tram
line.

00:01:20.349 --> 00:01:24.599
Robinson narrowly escaped death but was left
severely disfigured.

00:01:24.599 --> 00:01:28.090
He lost his nose, eyes, an ear and and one
of his arms.

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:33.520
The skin on his face was so badly damaged
by the shock that it glowed with a green hue.

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:36.249
Hence his nickname of The Green Man.

00:01:36.249 --> 00:01:41.280
Robinson walked the roads of western Pennsylvania
every night because he could not go outside

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.950
during the day without causing mass hysteria.

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:44.950
The Shadowy Figure

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:46.529
Next up is the shadowy figure.

00:01:46.529 --> 00:01:50.119
I'm sure that everyone has been witness to
this urban legend.

00:01:50.119 --> 00:01:55.149
At some point in most people's lives, they've
seen a shadowy figure dart across the room,

00:01:55.149 --> 00:01:56.810
out the corner of their eye.

00:01:56.810 --> 00:02:01.950
As if someone is there, but when they turn
around, nothing.

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:07.549
It's the oldest urban legend in the book and
stories of mysterious shadowy figures have

00:02:07.549 --> 00:02:09.840
been told all throughout history.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:13.060
But for one man in Fukuoka, Japan.

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:15.870
This urban legend turned out to be true.

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:19.560
The man, apparently, lived alone in an apartment.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:24.010
He kept telling people how he saw shadowy
figures moving around his apartment, out the

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:25.490
corner of his eye.

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:29.750
He swore that things kept going missing from
his apartment; the man claimed that someone

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:33.080
was eating his food and moving things around.

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:38.359
He reported an overwhelming sense that another
being was present with him and that he was

00:02:38.359 --> 00:02:40.250
far from alone.

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:42.989
He was absolutely correct.

00:02:42.989 --> 00:02:45.930
One day he set up a hidden camera in the corner
of his apartment.

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:51.980
And, to the man's horror, he captured footage
of a woman slithering out of his cupboard

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:54.700
and using his apartment as if it was hers.

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:59.640
Eating his food and using his belongings;
even taking showers.

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:03.709
The creepiest part of it all is that when
he was watching the footage back, the woman

00:03:03.709 --> 00:03:07.999
was still in his cupboard, only a few metres
behind him.

00:03:07.999 --> 00:03:12.799
The woman turned out to be 58-year-old Tatsuko
Horikawa.

00:03:12.799 --> 00:03:17.260
She was homeless and admitted to the police
that she had been secretly living in the man's

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:20.379
apartment, without his knowledge, for the
past year.

00:03:20.379 --> 00:03:21.379
Bloody Mary

00:03:21.379 --> 00:03:24.930
There's an old folklore called Bloody Mary,
that goes likes this.

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:30.019
If you turn off all the lights, then light
a candle and stare into a mirror and chant

00:03:30.019 --> 00:03:32.810
"Bloody Mary" three times.

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:39.239
The face of Queen Mary I of England will supposedly
appear in the mirror with a terrifyingly evil

00:03:39.239 --> 00:03:40.329
expression.

00:03:40.329 --> 00:03:44.790
In some versions of this urban legend, she
apparently appears in the mirror holding a

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:47.189
dead baby in her arms.

00:03:47.189 --> 00:03:52.080
Which may be a reference to the number of
miscarriages that Queen Mary I had.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:57.920
This may seem farfetched, but there is some
truth to this urban legend, and oddly enough,

00:03:57.920 --> 00:03:59.079
some science too.

00:03:59.079 --> 00:04:04.879
A lot of people who try this, do actually
see something peculiar in the mirror.

00:04:04.879 --> 00:04:10.200
And many perceive it to be the face of Queen
Mary I, but it's not.

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:14.599
What you're actually seeing is your own face
heavily distorted, due to something called

00:04:14.599 --> 00:04:16.340
the Caputo Effect.

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:18.979
This effect occurs because of sensory deprivation.

00:04:18.979 --> 00:04:23.840
Our eyes are being deprived of light, but
our brain is trying its hardest to make out

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:25.590
the face in the mirror.

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:29.710
This causes the brain's facial-recognition
system to malfunction.

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:36.389
The result of this is that we see a distorted
version of our own face, which, in poor lighting,

00:04:36.389 --> 00:04:40.490
could be misconstrued as the face of Queen
Mary.

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:45.440
Because most people who attempt this are expecting
to see the face of an evil Queen, that's what

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:47.069
the brain makes us see.

00:04:47.069 --> 00:04:53.560
Our brain is deprived of visual information,
so naturally, our imagination fills in the

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:54.560
gaps.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:55.560
Dead Body in the Mattress

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:59.090
There's an infamous story that many parents
have told their poor children in an attempt

00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:01.620
to scare the living daylights out of them.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:06.960
The legend goes that a couple stayed in a
hotel room and complained about a putrid smell.

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:12.889
But, when the hotel staff couldn't find anything
out of the ordinary, they stayed there anyway.

00:05:12.889 --> 00:05:18.419
Later, they found that the cause of the smell
was a dead body stuffed into the mattress.

00:05:18.419 --> 00:05:21.839
That's bloody nasty, but it has happened.

00:05:21.839 --> 00:05:26.120
In fact it happens a lot more commonly than
you might think.

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:30.940
Cases of dead bodies in hotel mattress's have
been reported in Las Vegas, Atlantic City,

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:32.460
California and Florida.

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:38.930
A recent case occurred in 2010 when a Memphis
woman was missing for two months before she

00:05:38.930 --> 00:05:44.880
was finally found, dead, under the mattress
of a hotel room she had been staying in.

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:49.729
In the two months whilst her corpse had been
rotting away under the mattress, the hotel

00:05:49.729 --> 00:05:54.740
had rented the room to five different people,
and none of them thought to investigate the

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:55.740
strange smell.

00:05:55.740 --> 00:06:00.690
The room had also been cleaned by hotel staff,
several times during those two months.

00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:04.980
I guess the cleaners just took one look at
the body and thought "I don't get paid enough

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:05.980
for this."

00:06:05.980 --> 00:06:06.980
Black Water

00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:11.230
According to urban legend, there's an unnerving
tale of a family who moved into a new house.

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:16.110
The story goes that a rancid smelling, jet-black
water came out of all the taps in their new

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:17.110
home.

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:22.050
When they investigated, they were horrified
to discover that the cause of the black water

00:06:22.050 --> 00:06:25.780
was a decomposing human body in their water
tank.

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:30.580
It makes one's skin crawl to think that this
could actually be true, but it is.

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:32.960
However the real story is so much worse.

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:36.569
Because it happened in a hotel, not someone's
home.

00:06:36.569 --> 00:06:43.879
In 2013, for a whole 19 days, hundreds of
guests at the Cecil Hotel in Los Angeles,

00:06:43.879 --> 00:06:48.790
were bathing in, brushing their teeth with
and even drinking the water from a tank on

00:06:48.790 --> 00:06:55.009
the rooftop that contained the decomposing
corpse of a college student named Elisa Lam.

00:06:55.009 --> 00:06:57.990
Seriously guys, just stay away from hotels,
they're bad news.

00:06:57.990 --> 00:06:58.990
Buried Alive

00:06:58.990 --> 00:07:03.759
We've all heard the horror stories of people
who have been buried, six feet under, presuming

00:07:03.759 --> 00:07:06.220
they were dead, but, they weren't.

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:10.539
Are the tales just urban myths, or is there
some truth to it?

00:07:10.539 --> 00:07:15.720
Unfortunately it's true and not only is it
true, but it's happened literally hundreds,

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:17.180
if not thousands of times.

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:23.160
In the late 19th century, when the medical
profession hadn't yet fully developed, people

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:26.130
were mistakingly buried alive quite regularly.

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:32.970
There were 219 known and reported cases of
people being buried alive during the late

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:33.970
19th century.

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:38.860
But that's just the ones that were later dug
up, only to find scratch marks on the inside

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:42.180
of the coffin where they tried to get out.

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:45.689
Just think how many more people this happened
to without anyone's knowledge.

00:07:45.689 --> 00:07:50.080
Because, you know, once you bury someone,
it's usually a permanent arrangement.

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:54.280
You don't usually make regular checkups to
see if Granddad is still alive down there.

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:59.580
In fact, this happened with such regularity
that wealthy people would invest in "safety

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:03.740
coffins" before they died, to prevent premature
burial.

00:08:03.740 --> 00:08:08.469
These specially built coffins had a device
that allowed the supposedly deceased person

00:08:08.469 --> 00:08:13.000
to ring a bell above the surface, if they
were still alive down there.

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:18.110
Some people believe this is where the phrases
"saved by the bell" and "dead ringer" come

00:08:18.110 --> 00:08:21.620
from, but there's still some debate going
on over this.

00:08:21.620 --> 00:08:26.060
Many designs of these safety coffins were
patented during the 18th and 19th centuries

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:28.639
and they sold in their thousands.

00:08:28.639 --> 00:08:33.250
You can still buy more modern versions of
safety coffins today for the ultra-paranoid

00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:34.250
out there.

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:35.250
Carnival Corpse

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:38.290
When you went on the haunted house ride at
the carnival as a child, did your parents

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:43.690
ever tell you that the paper mache corpse
handing up was actually a real human corpse?

00:08:43.690 --> 00:08:47.330
Well in at least one fairground this turned
out to be gruesomely true.

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:52.780
In 1976 a camera crew was filming an episode
of The Six Million Dollar Man at the Nu-Pike

00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:55.680
amusement park in Long Beach, California.

00:08:55.680 --> 00:09:00.550
The crew was moving a hanging man prop whilst
preparing to film inside the haunted house.

00:09:00.550 --> 00:09:04.710
When, they accidentally knocked off one of
its arms.

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:10.280
To their horror this prop wasn't made of paper
mache, because inside they found real human

00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:11.440
bones.

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:15.660
Turns out the whole thing was a real human
cadaver, hung up for all the little kiddies

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:16.660
to see.

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:18.930
It wasn't any ordinary corpse either.

00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:24.110
It turns out the body was that of a criminal
mastermind Elmer McCurdy, who was shot and

00:09:24.110 --> 00:09:27.470
killed whilst robbing a train in 1911.

00:09:27.470 --> 00:09:30.320
His body was embalmed by the local undertaker.

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:35.450
The undertaker was so pleased with his work
that he put it on display in his funeral home

00:09:35.450 --> 00:09:37.270
to show off to clients.

00:09:37.270 --> 00:09:41.090
Like some kind of horrible, macabre portfolio
of dead bodies.

00:09:41.090 --> 00:09:46.990
McCurdy's corpse remained on display in the
undertaker's funeral home for several years

00:09:46.990 --> 00:09:52.200
until one day McCurdy's brothers showed up
and claimed the corpse.

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:56.150
Turns out these guys weren't his brothers
at all, but carnival promoters who were too

00:09:56.150 --> 00:10:00.080
lazy to make their own artificial props for
the haunted house ride.

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:05.460
McCurdy's corpse went on a whirlwind carnival
tour all across America, scaring the holy

00:10:05.460 --> 00:10:08.220
hell out of little kids everywhere it went.

00:10:08.220 --> 00:10:13.640
Until it was finally discovered by the film
crew in Long Beach, California, and he was

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:14.640
finally buried.

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:15.710
Insects Infesting Your Brain

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:21.370
There's hundreds of urban legends about people
who get a creepy crawly inside their ear and

00:10:21.370 --> 00:10:24.740
the bug then lays its eggs inside their skull.

00:10:24.740 --> 00:10:30.100
Well I truly am sorry to tell you this, because
after hearing it you will probably never go

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:31.300
outside again.

00:10:31.300 --> 00:10:32.890
But it does happen.

00:10:32.890 --> 00:10:40.940
It happens very rarely, but one recent case
happened in 2013 to Rochelle Harris from Derby,

00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:41.940
England.

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:46.850
She was on the flight back from a holiday
in Peru when she began to develop headaches.

00:10:46.850 --> 00:10:51.000
She ignored them until a few hours later when
she started to get shooting pains down the

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:52.780
side of her face.

00:10:52.780 --> 00:10:58.870
Then to her absolute horror, she heard scratching
sounds inside her own head.

00:10:58.870 --> 00:11:04.700
The next morning she woke up to a pillow soaked
in fluid which was pouring out of her ear.

00:11:04.700 --> 00:11:07.230
Harris went to the hospital in Derby.

00:11:07.230 --> 00:11:11.300
After a brain x-ray the doctor told her she
had maggots living inside her ear canal.

00:11:11.300 --> 00:11:16.640
At which point she instantly burst into tears,
rightfully so.

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:22.050
The maggots had burrowed a hole 12mm deep
into her ear canal, luckily they hadn't yet

00:11:22.050 --> 00:11:25.020
reached her brain and caused any serious damage.

00:11:25.020 --> 00:11:28.290
Harris had minor surgery to remove the maggots.

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:33.930
The surgeons found a colony of 8 large flesh
eating maggots inside her ear.

00:11:33.930 --> 00:11:38.460
After laboratory research it was discovered
that the maggots must have hatched in her

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:44.740
ear after a Screw-Worm Fly had flown into
her ear and laid its eggs, whilst she was

00:11:44.740 --> 00:11:45.770
in Peru.

00:11:45.770 --> 00:11:50.760
So if there's anything you can take away from
this video, it's that if you ever go to Peru,

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:51.760
cover your ears.

00:11:51.760 --> 00:11:54.350
Also, don't stay in hotels, ever.

00:11:54.350 --> 00:11:58.820
Check all your cupboards in your house because
there might be someone living in there.

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:03.630
Oh, and if you ever go to a carnival, don't
touch the props.

